
# ML Pathway - Phase 0 Setup

> [!abstract] Phase purpose
> Phase 0 creates the minimum viable training infrastructure for the ML Pathway. It is not a learning phase, not a template-polishing phase, and not a platform-engineering phase. The only acceptable outcome is a reusable lab skeleton that can run tests, train a deterministic smoke model, evaluate that model, track the lifecycle with MLflow, and safely create-benchmark-destroy DigitalOcean GPU machines without leaving billable GPU infrastructure behind.

**Binding rule:** DigitalOcean GPU work must survive operator failure. Forgetting to destroy a GPU droplet is an expected event, not an edge case.

**Safety contract:** No matter which path runs — happy path, Ctrl-C, SIGKILL, terminal loss, timeout, manual down, recurring self-destruct, duplicate destroy, or already-destroyed recovery — success means the droplet does not exist and audit is clean. Everything else is implementation detail.

**Source alignment:** The converged [[ML Pathway - Master Plan|master plan]] locks Phase 0 to five outputs: repo skeleton, `make test` / `make train` / `make evaluate`, local MLflow, a dummy model lifecycle, and DigitalOcean GPU provisioning/teardown automation. This note implements those outputs and does not reopen locked decisions.

